{"abstract":"In robotics, echolocation has been used to detect acoustic reflectors, e.g., walls, as it aids the robotic platform to navigate in darkness and also helps detect transparent surfaces. However, the transfer function or response of an acoustic system, e.g., loudspeakers/emitters, contributes to non-ideal behavior within the acoustic systems that can contribute to a phase lag due to propagation delay. This non-ideal response can hinder the performance of a time-of-arrival (TOA) estimator intended for acoustic reflector localization especially when the estimation of multiple reflections is required. In this paper, we, therefore, propose a robust expectation-maximization (EM) algorithm that takes into account the response of acoustic systems to enhance the TOA estimation accuracy when estimating multiple reflections when the robot is placed in a corner of a room. A non-ideal transfer function is built with two parameters, which are estimated recursively within the estimator. To test the proposed method, a hardware proof-of-concept setup was built with two different designs. The experimental results show that the proposed method could detect an acoustic reflector up to a distance of 1.6 m with 60% accuracy under the signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) of 0 dB. Compared to the state-of-the-art EM algorithm, our proposed method provides improved performance when estimating TOA by 10% under a low SNR value.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Saqib, Usama","Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","Jensen, Jesper Rindom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-743120"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Saqib, Usama"],"keyword":["Active source localization","DOA estimation","Expectation maximization","Prewhitening","Robot drone audition","TOA estimation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"robust acoustic reflector localization using a modified em algorithm","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13636-024-00340-y","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-743120","identifier":[{"id":"85190867144","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-ab874cb9-0b62-4e8a-b97d-70e3e8a2fa0d"],"keyword":["Active source localization","DOA estimation","Expectation-maximization","Prewhitening","Robot/drone audition","TOA estimation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5CB03ED0F306A078FC5FB7E293A06D25"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13636-024-00340-y","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Usama","key":"saqibpau","last":"Saqib","locid":"7476d818-5c13-4793-a06c-491b5190c52e","name":"Saqib, Usama","orcid":"0000-0001-9783-1887","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Græsbøll","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"cf9e922d-e5f8-4964-9b84-581667f97b0b","name":"Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","orcid":"0000-0003-3586-7969","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Rindom","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"af897213-5e0d-41e9-8e3c-a89d3ca4a5b1","name":"Jensen, Jesper Rindom","name_org":"Jensen, Jesper Rindom","orcid":"0000-0001-6023-8270","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13636-024-00340-y","issn":["16874714","16874722"],"issn_org":["16874714"],"journal":"Eurasip Journal on Audio, Speech, and Music Processing","paperid":"22","publisher":"Springer Publishing Company","status":"p","title":"Eurasip Journal on Audio, Speech, and Music Processing","volume":"2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85190867144"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ab874cb9-0b62-4e8a-b97d-70e3e8a2fa0d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Robust acoustic reflector localization using a modified EM algorithm","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-743120","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Saqib, Usama"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-667139"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Acoustics","Beamforming","Direction of arrival DOA estimation","Drones","Robotics","room geometry estimation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"acoustic echo estimation using the model based approach with application to spatial map construction in robotics","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.54337/aau528831183","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-667139","ids":["aau-320a2dd8-fdd5-47b3-a106-fffbef13440e"],"keyword":["acoustics","beamforming","direction of arrival (DOA) estimation","drones","robotics","room geometry estimation","time of arrival (TOA) estimation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6C6CEC35DD9987DF5C9F5C89195C8B38"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.54337/aau528831183","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/549499513/PHD_US.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Audio Analysis Lab (CREATE)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Usama","key":"saqibpau","last":"Saqib","locid":"7476d818-5c13-4793-a06c-491b5190c52e","name":"Saqib, Usama","orcid":"0000-0001-9783-1887","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.54337/aau528831183","issn":["24461628"],"pages":"192","publisher":"Aalborg Universitetsforlag","series":"Ph.d.-serien for Det Tekniske Fakultet for IT og Design, Aalborg Universitet","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-320a2dd8-fdd5-47b3-a106-fffbef13440e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Acoustic Echo Estimation using the model-based approach with Application to Spatial Map Construction in Robotics","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-667139","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we propose a method to estimate the proximity of an acoustic reflector, e.g., a wall, using ego-noise, i.e., the noise produced by the moving parts of a listening robot. This is achieved by estimating the times of arrival of acoustic echoes reflected from the surface. Simulated experiments show that the proposed non-intrusive approach is capable of accurately estimating the distance of a reflector up to 1 meter and outperforms a previously proposed intrusive approach under loud ego-noise conditions. The proposed method is helped by a probabilistic echo detector that estimates whether or not an acoustic reflector is within a short range of the robotic platform. This preliminary investigation paves the way towards a new kind of collision avoidance system that would purely rely on audio sensors rather than conventional proximity sensors.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Saqib, Usama","Deleforge, Antoine","Jensen, Jesper Rindom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-077755"],"event":{"acronym":"ICASSP","end":"2021-06-11","place":"Toronto, ca","start":"2021-06-06","title":"ICASSP 2021 - 2021 IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (ICASSP)","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Université de Lorraine"],"keyword":["Robot drone audition","Robotics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"detecting acoustic reflectors using a robot s ego noise","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2111.08327.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-077755","identifier":[{"id":"85115144868","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-5f65023d-5e53-4236-93e1-e8c2dfef1609"],"keyword":["Echo detection","Ego-noise","Robot/Drone audition","Robotics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-64B05351A69BC9D73627D7DDBFE98199"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2111.08327.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Aalborg"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"université de lorraine","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Université de Lorraine","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Usama","key":"saqibpau","last":"Saqib","locid":"7476d818-5c13-4793-a06c-491b5190c52e","name":"Saqib, Usama","orcid":"0000-0001-9783-1887","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Antoine","key":"deleforgepau","last":"Deleforge","name":"Deleforge, Antoine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Rindom","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"af897213-5e0d-41e9-8e3c-a89d3ca4a5b1","name":"Jensen, Jesper Rindom","orcid":"0000-0001-6023-8270","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/icassp39728.2021.9414061","eisbn":["9781728176055"],"isbn":["9781728176062"],"issn":["15206149"],"pages":"466-470","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","series":"IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing. Proceedings","status":"p","title":"International Conference on Acoustic, Speech and Signal Processing","volume":"2021-June"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85115144868"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5f65023d-5e53-4236-93e1-e8c2dfef1609"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Detecting Acoustic Reflectors using a Robot's Ego-noise","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-077755","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"In this work, we present a framework for constructing a spatial map of an indoor environment using the concept of echolocation. More specifically, we propose a non-linear least squares (NLS) estimator which is combined with a spatial filtering technique, e.g., beamforming, to estimate both the time-of-arrival (TOA) and direction-of-arrival (DOA) of the acoustic echoes. The proposed framework is complemented with an echo detector to classify a spurious estimate and an acoustic reflector, i.e., a wall. Based on these estimators, we then propose two algorithms that can complement existing range sensors and aid a robotic platform in acoustic reflector localization and mapping: a singlechannel localization and mapping (ScLAM) and a multi-channel localization and mapping (McLAM). Compared to commonly used sensors, e.g., lidar and cameras, our proposed method can detect transparent surfaces that are typically found in an office environment. To test our algorithms, a proof-of-concept robotic platform was built. According to our evaluation, both qualitative and quantitative experiments reveal that the proposed methods can detect an acoustic reflector up to a distance of 1.5 m at a signal-to-diffuse-noise ratio (SDNR) of 0 dB in a simulated environment and 10 dB in a real environment with an accuracy of 80 %.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Saqib, Usama","Jensen, Jesper Rindom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-061142"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a framework for spatial map generation using acoustic echoes for robotic platforms","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dpr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"rem","url":"https://hal.archives-ouvertes.fr/hal-03198131/document","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-061142","ids":["aau-262f3318-a9f1-4da3-aa1e-42e435578294"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8B7CE09EC82DE3E3AE0A6B6958A9D0AF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"rem","url":"https://hal.archives-ouvertes.fr/hal-03198131/document","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Audio Analysis Lab (CREATE)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Aalborg"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Usama","key":"saqibpau","last":"Saqib","locid":"7476d818-5c13-4793-a06c-491b5190c52e","name":"Saqib, Usama","orcid":"0000-0001-9783-1887","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Rindom","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"af897213-5e0d-41e9-8e3c-a89d3ca4a5b1","name":"Jensen, Jesper Rindom","orcid":"0000-0001-6023-8270","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"16","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-262f3318-a9f1-4da3-aa1e-42e435578294"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A Framework for Spatial map Generation using Acoustic Echoes for Robotic Platforms","type":"Preprint","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-061142","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The transfer function or response of an acoustic system, e.g., loudspeakers, contributes to a phase lag due to propagation delay that can hinder the performance of a time-of-arrival (TOA) estimator intended for acoustic reflector localization using echolocation. In this paper, we propose a Robust Expectation-Maximization (EM) algorithm that takes into account the response of acoustic systems to enhance the TOA estimation accuracy. To test the proposed method, a hardware proof-of-concept setup was built with two different designs. The experimental results show that the proposed method could detect an acoustic reflector up to a distance of 1.6 m with 60% accuracy under the signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) of 0 dB. Moreover, we also show that the proposed method can also be used to estimate multiple acoustic echoes that originate when a robot is placed at a corner of a room.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Saqib, Usama","Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","Jensen, Jesper Rindom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-118811"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"robust acoustic reflector localization for robots","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"rem","url":"https://hal.archives-ouvertes.fr/hal-03154438/document","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-118811","ids":["aau-ec8fdb7c-c92c-49c6-b4a7-495185da8843"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6DA01D5852F4931676E9C6C501F81EFF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"rem","url":"https://hal.archives-ouvertes.fr/hal-03154438/document","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Audio Analysis Lab (CREATE)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Aalborg"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Usama","key":"saqibpau","last":"Saqib","locid":"7476d818-5c13-4793-a06c-491b5190c52e","name":"Saqib, Usama","orcid":"0000-0001-9783-1887","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Græsbøll","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"cf9e922d-e5f8-4964-9b84-581667f97b0b","name":"Christensen, Mads Græsbøll","orcid":"0000-0003-3586-7969","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Rindom","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"af897213-5e0d-41e9-8e3c-a89d3ca4a5b1","name":"Jensen, Jesper Rindom","orcid":"0000-0001-6023-8270","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"8","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ec8fdb7c-c92c-49c6-b4a7-495185da8843"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Robust Acoustic Reflector Localization for Robots","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-118811","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Constructing a spatial map of an indoor environment, e.g., a typical office environment with glass surfaces, is a difficult and challenging task. Current state-of-the-art, e.g., camera- and laser-based approaches are unsuitable for detecting transparent surfaces. Hence, the spatial map generated with these approaches are often inaccurate. In this paper, a method that utilizes echolocation with sound in the audible frequency range is proposed to robustly localize the position of an acoustic reflector, e.g., walls, glass surfaces etc., which could be used to construct a spatial map of an indoor environment as the robot moves. The proposed method estimate the acoustic reflector’s position, using only a single microphone and a loudspeaker that are present on many socially assistive robot platforms such as the NAO robot. The experimentalesults show that the proposed method could robustly detect an acoustic reflector up to a distance of 1.5 m in more than 60% of the trials and works efficiently even under low SNRs. To test the proposed method, a proof-of-concept robotic platform was build to construct a spatial map of an indoor environment.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Saqib, Usama","Jensen, Jesper Rindom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-117413"],"event":{"acronym":"IROS","end":"2020-10-30","place":"Las Vegas, us","start":"2020-10-24","title":"2020 IEEE/RSJ International Conference on Intelligent Robots and Systems","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Array processing","Mapping","TOA estimation","robot audition"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a model based approach to acoustic reflector localization with a robotic platform","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-117413","identifier":[{"id":"85102413840","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-e7b7a1f9-d4ba-40a1-a2ac-f33c016b8357"],"keyword":["Array Processing","TOA estimation","acoustic echoes","mapping","robot audition"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8395DFC3DAE26A31BDEB5E5107AE885A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Audio Analysis Lab (CREATE)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Aalborg"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Usama","key":"saqibpau","last":"Saqib","locid":"7476d818-5c13-4793-a06c-491b5190c52e","name":"Saqib, Usama","orcid":"0000-0001-9783-1887","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Rindom","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"af897213-5e0d-41e9-8e3c-a89d3ca4a5b1","name":"Jensen, Jesper Rindom","orcid":"0000-0001-6023-8270","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/iros45743.2020.9341437","eisbn":["9781728162119"],"pages":"4499-4504","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"A model-based approach to acoustic reflector localization with a robotic platform"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85102413840"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e7b7a1f9-d4ba-40a1-a2ac-f33c016b8357"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A model-based approach to acoustic reflector localization with a robotic platform","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-117413","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Estimation problems like room geometry estimation and localization of acoustic reflectors are of great interest and importance in robot and drone audition. Several methods for tackling these problems exist, but most of them rely on information about times-of-arrival (TOAs) of the acoustic echoes. These need to be estimated in practice, which is a difficult problem in itself, especially in robot applications which are characterized by high ego-noise. Moreover, even if TOAs are successfully extracted, the difficult problem of echolabeling needs to be solved. In this paper, we propose multiple expectation-maximization (EM) methods, for jointly estimating the TOAs and directions-of-arrival (DOA) of the echoes, with a uniform circular array (UCA) and a loudspeaker in its center for probing the environment. The different methods are derived to be optimal under different noise conditions. The experimental results show that the proposed methods outperform existing methods in terms of estimation accuracy in noisy conditions. For example, it can provide accurate estimates at SNR of 10 dB lower compared to TOA extraction from room impulse responses, which is often used. Furthermore, the results confirm that the proposed methods can account for scenarios with colored noise or faulty microphones. Finally, we show the applicability of the proposed methods in mapping of an indoor environment.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Saqib, Usama","Gannot, Sharon","Jensen, Jesper Rindom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-112279"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Jensen, Jesper Rindom"],"keyword":["Active source localization","DOA estimation","Expectation maximization","Prewhitening","Robot drone audition","TOA estimation","robot audition"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"estimation of acoustic echoes using expectation maximization methods","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13636-020-00179-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-112279","identifier":[{"id":"85089232159","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-d635100a-a9e8-4d2b-9578-edb547ce7171"],"keyword":["Acoustic reflector estimation","Active source localization","DOA estimation","Drones Audition","Expectation-maximization","Prewhitening","Robot/drone audition","TOA estimation","robot audition"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8341F105E1476B3CECF53FE69907CBDB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/406031072/s13636_020_00179_z.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13636-020-00179-z","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Audio Analysis Lab (CREATE)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Aalborg"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Usama","key":"saqibpau","last":"Saqib","locid":"7476d818-5c13-4793-a06c-491b5190c52e","name":"Saqib, Usama","orcid":"0000-0001-9783-1887","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sharon","key":"gannotpau","last":"Gannot","locid":"b6113cce-0f13-4563-9e3b-9dba53fa7804","name":"Gannot, Sharon","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Rindom","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"af897213-5e0d-41e9-8e3c-a89d3ca4a5b1","name":"Jensen, Jesper Rindom","orcid":"0000-0001-6023-8270","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13636-020-00179-z","issn":["16874714","16874722"],"issn_org":["16874714"],"issue":"1","journal":"Eurasip Journal on Audio, Speech, and Music Processing","paperid":"12","publisher":"Springer Publishing Company","status":"p","title":"Eurasip Journal on Audio, Speech, and Music Processing","volume":"2020"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089232159"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d635100a-a9e8-4d2b-9578-edb547ce7171"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Estimation of acoustic echoes using expectation-maximization methods","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-112279","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"An off-the-shelf drone for indoor operation wouldcome with a variety of different sensors that are used concur-rently to avoid collision with, e.g., walls, but these sensors are typically uni-directional and offers limited spatial awareness. In this paper, we propose a model-based technique for distance estimation using sound and its reflections. More specifically, the technique is estimating Time-of-Arrivals (TOAs) of the reflected sound that could infer knowledge about room geometry and help in the design of sound-based collision avoidance. Our proposed solution is thus based on probing a known sound into an environment and then estimating the TOAs of reflected sounds recorded by a single microphone. The simulated results show that our approach to estimating TOAs for reflector position estimation works up to a distance of at least 2 meters even with significant additive noise, e.g., drone ego noise.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Saqib, Usama","Jensen, Jesper Rindom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-050300"],"event":{"acronym":"Eusipco","end":"2019-09-06","place":"Coruña, es","start":"2019-09-02","title":"27th European Signal Processing Conference, EUSIPCO 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Robotics","room geometry estimation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sound based distance estimation for indoor navigation in the presence of ego noise","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"rem","url":"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/8902694","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-050300","identifier":[{"id":"85075616793","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-00e71520-99a7-493b-a808-268923da2025"],"keyword":["Acoustics impulse response","robotics","room geometry estimation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6B9BD365AD101D3F19FD804977D10487"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"rem","url":"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/8902694","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/323028807/1570534429.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Audio Analysis Lab (CREATE)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Usama","key":"saqibpau","last":"Saqib","locid":"7476d818-5c13-4793-a06c-491b5190c52e","name":"Saqib, Usama","orcid":"0000-0001-9783-1887","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Rindom","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"af897213-5e0d-41e9-8e3c-a89d3ca4a5b1","name":"Jensen, Jesper Rindom","orcid":"0000-0001-6023-8270","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.23919/eusipco.2019.8902694","eisbn":["9789082797039"],"isbn":["9789082797022 (USB)"],"issn":["20761465"],"publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","series":"European Signal Processing Conference","status":"p","title":"2019 27th European Signal Processing Conference (EUSIPCO)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85075616793"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-00e71520-99a7-493b-a808-268923da2025"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Sound-based Distance Estimation for Indoor Navigation in the Presence of Ego Noise","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-050300","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The time-of-arrivals (TOAs) of acoustic echoes is a prerequisite in, e.g., room geometry estimation and localization of acoustic reflectors, which can be an enabling technology for autonomous robots and drones. However, solving these problems alone using TOAs introduces the difficult problem of echolabeling. Moreover, it is typically suggested to estimate the TOAs by estimating the room impulse response, and finding the peaks of it, but this approach is vulnerable against noise (e.g., ego noise). We therefore propose an expectation-maximization (EM) method for estimating both the TOAs and direction-of-arrivals (DOAs) of acoustic echoes using a loudspeaker and a uniform circular array (UCA). Our results show that this approach is more robust against noise compared to the traditional peak finding approach. Moreover, they show that the TOA and DOA information can be combined to estimate wall positions directly without considering echolabeling.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jensen, Jesper Rindom","Saqib, Usama","Gannot, Sharon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-102537"],"event":{"acronym":"WASPAA","end":"2020-01-23","place":"New Paltz, us","start":"2019-10-20","title":"IEEE Workshop on Applications of Signal Processing to Audio and Acoustics 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Expectation maximization","Microphone arrays","TOA estimation","active localization","robot and drone audition"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an em method for multichannel toa and doa estimation of acoustic echoes","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85078069938&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-102537","identifier":[{"id":"85078069938","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-b4ad3c2c-356a-4a95-8794-935103602a30"],"keyword":["TOA estimation","active localization","expectation-maximization","microphone arrays","robot and drone audition"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0B81DA093BABFCCC0206A40A83EF110F"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Audio Analysis Lab (CREATE)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Aalborg"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Rindom","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"af897213-5e0d-41e9-8e3c-a89d3ca4a5b1","name":"Jensen, Jesper Rindom","orcid":"0000-0001-6023-8270","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Usama","key":"saqibpau","last":"Saqib","locid":"7476d818-5c13-4793-a06c-491b5190c52e","name":"Saqib, Usama","orcid":"0000-0001-9783-1887","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sharon","key":"gannotpau","last":"Gannot","locid":"b6113cce-0f13-4563-9e3b-9dba53fa7804","name":"Gannot, Sharon","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/waspaa.2019.8937252","eisbn":["9781728111230"],"issn":["19471629"],"pages":"120-124","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","series":"IEEE Workshop on Applications of Signal Processing to Audio and Acoustics","status":"p","title":"2019 IEEE Workshop on Applications of Signal Processing to Audio and Acoustics (WASPAA)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85078069938"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b4ad3c2c-356a-4a95-8794-935103602a30"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"An EM Method for Multichannel TOA and DOA Estimation of Acoustic Echoes","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-102537","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
